    <ns1:definition xml:lang="en">Observe the damage on the plants caused by brown planthopper. For a field test, use an augmented experimental design with a susceptible check replicated at intervals across the whole trial. The test is considered a valid test for resistance if the hopper population is uniformly distributed at a high level across the screening box, as indicated by hopper counts on the susceptible check. A minimum of the following hopper density on susceptible check is necessary: a. 10 hoppers/hill at 10-15 days after transplanting, b. 25 hoppers / hiII at maximum tillering, c. 100 hoppers/hill at early booting stage</ns1:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <ns2:Restriction rdf:nodeID="Nb3f3a5a6a98449769406a58ac8e4cb39">
